15:00.367 --> 15:01.307
Sunshine Girl?

15:01.307 --> 15:02.357
I'm a Sunshine Girl!

15:02.357 --> 15:04.477
It's raining so much this year.

15:04.477 --> 15:05.327
He ignored me?

15:05.327 --> 15:07.307
There's a demand for that.

15:07.437 --> 15:08.257
Right...

15:08.567 --> 15:11.237
Come on, you've
got zero initiative.

15:11.237 --> 15:14.517
She's got an interview appointment.
Go along and listen.

15:14.517 --> 15:16.567
Huh? Me? Right now?

15:16.657 --> 15:18.017
You're on probation!

15:18.017 --> 15:18.827
An intern.

15:19.127 --> 15:21.887
No, really. I can't...

15:22.957 --> 15:25.777
Of course, sunshine girls do exist.

15:25.777 --> 15:26.827
I knew it!

15:26.987 --> 15:29.337
And also rain girls.

15:29.147 --> 15:35.657
Psychic

15:30.117 --> 15:32.787
Sunshine girls are
possessed by a fox god.

15:32.787 --> 15:35.747
And rain girls are possessed
by a dragon god.

15:36.017 --> 15:37.097
Hm? Yes?

15:37.097 --> 15:41.917
Dragon god individuals drink a lot.
They yearn for water.

15:42.507 --> 15:45.577
They're strong-willed and competitive,
but a bit careless and unreliable.

15:45.807 --> 15:47.607
Huh, maybe that's me.

15:47.747 --> 15:52.387
Fox god individuals are hardworking,
but too weak-hearted to be leaders.

15:52.387 --> 15:53.507
Many are beautiful.

15:53.507 --> 15:54.857
That's me.

15:54.857 --> 15:59.917
The weather is off-balance now,
so more sunshine and rain girls are born.

15:59.987 --> 16:01.587
The Gaia homeostasis hypothesis.

16:01.587 --> 16:02.707
I see~

16:02.707 --> 16:05.017
But, we must be careful.

16:05.327 --> 16:09.327
Messing with nature
always has a cost.

16:09.327 --> 16:13.407
Whoever uses too much weather
power, gets spirited away.

16:13.407 --> 16:14.267
That's...

16:14.227 --> 16:18.727
Psychic

16:15.467 --> 16:17.267
I will be careful.

16:18.317 --> 16:20.267
So, how was it?

16:22.187 --> 16:26.957
A so-called psychic talked at length
about fantasy novel like stuff.

16:26.957 --> 16:29.167
If you use too much power,
you'll get spirited away.

16:29.167 --> 16:30.487
I see. That kinda stuff.

16:30.587 --> 16:32.757
Weather isn't some kind of power.

16:32.757 --> 16:35.487
It's a natural phenomenon.

16:35.487 --> 16:40.917
Look, I know but we're
providing entertainment here.

16:40.917 --> 16:43.687
Is that all you've written
so far? Slow...

16:43.687 --> 16:44.347
Sorry.

16:44.347 --> 16:47.257
Aah, but it's not bad.

16:48.167 --> 16:49.837
All right boy, you're hired!

16:49.837 --> 16:51.917
Wait a minute!
I didn't say I was...

16:51.917 --> 16:53.477
It's a live-in job.

16:54.567 --> 16:55.317
With meals.

16:55.317 --> 16:56.317
Really?

16:56.377 --> 16:57.777
I'll do it! Please hire me!

16:57.777 --> 17:01.117
Good. What's your name again?

17:01.117 --> 17:02.537
You're funny!

17:02.537 --> 17:03.647
It's Hodaka-kun, right?

17:03.647 --> 17:04.327
Right.

17:04.537 --> 17:05.607
There!

17:06.027 --> 17:07.077
Here.

17:07.737 --> 17:09.407
I'm underage.

17:10.097 --> 17:13.267
Let's celebrate Hodaka's hiring.

17:14.287 --> 17:15.997
Cheers!

17:19.097 --> 17:23.327
That was the first meal I shared
with someone since I came to Tokyo.

17:23.947 --> 17:27.307
This is when my new life started.

17:39.967 --> 17:41.977
Alarm

17:40.137 --> 17:44.447
kaze ga bokura no mae de kyuu ni kaji wo
The wind suddenly blew in front of us

17:44.447 --> 17:48.207
kitta no wo kanjita gogo
I felt it on that afternoon

17:48.207 --> 17:52.447
ima nara donna mucha mo sekai kiroku
Now I can do any craziness or any world record

17:52.447 --> 17:56.837
mo kikite to gyaku de daseru you na
Even with my opposite hand

17:56.837 --> 18:00.687
ki ga shitan da honki deshitan da 
I seriously felt like that

18:01.137 --> 18:05.357
It was a small editorial company run
only by Suga-san and Natsumi-san.

18:04.017 --> 18:07.917
'nan to ka naru sa' to 'ato dore kurai?'
"We'll manage it somehow" and "How much more?"

18:05.357 --> 18:07.217
I did all the office chores.

18:07.917 --> 18:11.077
to 'daijoubu ka na bokura'
And "Are we all right?"

18:08.017 --> 18:10.517
Starting from Suga-san's personal care...

18:10.517 --> 18:14.277
Answering the phone, filling
receipts, transcribing interviews.

18:11.077 --> 18:16.047
no aida wo, furiko no you ni ittari kitari shite wa
We're swinging between these like a pendulum

18:16.027 --> 18:18.057
Is that all you've written so far?

18:16.047 --> 18:18.777
te wo tsuyoku tsukanda
Holding hands tightly

18:18.057 --> 18:19.967
This isn't mine.

18:19.967 --> 18:21.837
Suga-san is out of office...

18:20.037 --> 18:23.827
isso kono yume no domannaka de hade ni
Rather, slowly in the middle of this dream

18:23.797 --> 18:28.617
With Natsumi-san's bike,
sometimes we rode around town.

18:23.827 --> 18:27.047
tsukaihatashite miyou yo 
Let's use up everything

18:30.037 --> 18:33.217
warawarenai kurai no ai de
If with love that no one would laugh at

18:34.317 --> 18:37.467
kaerareru kurai no sekai naraba
The world could be changed

18:37.467 --> 18:41.517
hajime kara you nado nai boku ni wa hitsuyou nai 
It had no use from the beginning, I don't need that

18:38.177 --> 18:39.467
Kindergartener, little girl
6 gossips from her
sis' friends in class?

A middle schooler?

18:41.517 --> 18:45.787
kami-sama hayaku tsugi wo boku ni kure yo 
Dear God, please give me the next one quickly

18:45.447 --> 18:47.677
They're looking for a sunshine girl.

18:46.227 --> 18:49.167
mittomonai kurai no koe de
With my horrible voice

18:47.677 --> 18:48.707
Really? That's hilarious.

18:48.707 --> 18:53.797
My sis' friend is a real sunshine girl.
She calls her the day before a date...

18:50.197 --> 18:53.487
arienai kurai no kono kimochi wo
I want to express this impossible feeling

18:53.487 --> 18:57.547
boku ni sakebasete yo, kusarasenaide yo
Let me shout, don't leave me behind

18:53.777 --> 18:55.777
Weather
Research
Lab

18:53.797 --> 18:55.867
We're not interested.

18:55.867 --> 19:00.177
Then, the weather balloon's videosonde
picked up something strange.

18:57.547 --> 19:02.157
bokura no moteamashita yuuki wo tsukawa sete yo
Let me use all of our courage we have

19:00.187 --> 19:03.157
A swarm of moving objects
among the cumulonimbi.

19:02.157 --> 19:05.327
warawarenai kurai no ai de
If with love that no one would laugh at

19:04.167 --> 19:06.207
Is that all you've written?

19:06.207 --> 19:07.907
Why didn't you get a discount?

19:06.247 --> 19:09.387
kaerareru kurai no sekai naraba
The world could be changed

19:07.907 --> 19:09.447
He's out of office...

19:09.447 --> 19:10.467
This paragraph is crap.

19:09.507 --> 19:13.647
hajime kara you nado nai boku ni wa hitsuyou nai 
It had no use from the beginning, I don't need that

19:10.467 --> 19:10.807
Yes.

19:10.807 --> 19:11.847
But this ain't bad.

19:11.847 --> 19:12.397
Yes.

19:12.297 --> 19:15.047
New Machine

19:12.297 --> 19:15.047
Front row

19:13.647 --> 19:18.037
bokura no moteamashita seigi wo tsukawasete
Let me use all of our extra justice we have

19:15.327 --> 19:18.567
Suga-san, come on, wake up.

19:18.037 --> 19:22.037
'sayonara' no nai haroo to 'shikatanai' no nai mirai to
 A hello without "good bye", a future without "despair"

19:22.037 --> 19:25.887
kagi no nai doa darake no kokoro de 
A heart with lots of door but no keys

19:23.507 --> 19:25.497
My days were hectic.

19:25.497 --> 19:29.197
But, for the first time,
someone was relying on me.

19:25.887 --> 19:30.047
mirai ga tokuige ni bokura wo mite kitemo dou demo ii ya
Even if the future looks proudly on us, it doesn't matter

19:30.047 --> 19:33.547
mada bokura nya yaru koto ga aru kara
We still have things to do

19:30.207 --> 19:34.047
And then, those rainy days in
Tokyo, passed in a flash!

19:33.547 --> 19:39.467
bokura no koboresou na kiseki wo tsukawasete yo
Let me use our miracle to the fullest

19:50.887 --> 19:51.897
Rain
(Ame)

19:52.577 --> 19:53.257
Rain
(Ame)

19:53.697 --> 19:54.377
Rain
(Ame)

19:54.647 --> 19:55.657
Rain
(Ame)

19:56.747 --> 19:57.927
There you are.

19:59.047 --> 20:01.547
How's it going, Ame?

20:02.087 --> 20:04.007
Yeah? Good boy.

20:07.107 --> 20:10.157
It's an easy job,
you'll see, don't worry.

20:10.157 --> 20:11.027
But...

20:13.237 --> 20:16.667
Just give it a try.
You'll get paid right away.

20:16.847 --> 20:18.967
Our club is right there.

20:21.097 --> 20:22.347
That girl...

20:27.407 --> 20:31.237
Give it a go, and
earn yourself some bucks.

20:33.397 --> 20:36.397
It's right there.
Let's go!

20:38.867 --> 20:40.287
But...

20:50.587 --> 20:51.827
Let's go!

20:53.467 --> 20:56.217
Hey... Wait a minute!

21:02.257 --> 21:03.127
Wait, you...

21:03.127 --> 21:04.297
Just keep running!

21:04.297 --> 21:06.097
Listen to me!

21:09.837 --> 21:11.677
You brat!

21:13.387 --> 21:16.237
Hey hey hey, you

21:16.567 --> 21:18.467
What do you think you're doing?

21:20.067 --> 21:21.257
You were forcing her.

21:21.257 --> 21:22.317
Huuh?

21:22.317 --> 21:23.517
Are you dumb?

21:23.517 --> 21:26.007
We've made a deal.

21:29.667 --> 21:31.057
Don't tell me...

21:31.647 --> 21:35.497
You're the brat that was
crouching in front of our club?

21:35.497 --> 21:38.067
What's this, a payback?

21:38.787 --> 21:40.467
Please, stop it!

21:41.207 --> 21:43.117
Damn...

21:44.117 --> 21:45.367
Get off me!

21:47.737 --> 21:49.967
What's that? A toy gun?

21:50.377 --> 21:52.547
You really are dumb.

22:16.867 --> 22:18.067
Get up!

22:42.647 --> 22:43.887
You...

22:44.927 --> 22:47.927
What was that for?
To thank me that burger?

22:49.207 --> 22:52.317
Where did you get that gun?
Who are you?

22:52.597 --> 22:53.967
That's...

22:53.967 --> 22:56.177
I found it. I thought it was a toy.

22:56.177 --> 22:58.647
It was like a lucky charm for me.

22:58.807 --> 22:59.937
What?

23:00.087 --> 23:01.717
You pointed it at that guy!

23:01.717 --> 23:03.367
You could have killed him!

23:04.377 --> 23:08.037
I can't believe it! You make
me sick! You are the worst!

23:42.457 --> 23:46.227
I... got fired from
my part-time job...

23:46.227 --> 23:47.807
Was it my fault?

23:47.807 --> 23:50.767
No, nothing to do
with that burger.

23:50.767 --> 23:52.067
But, that's why...

23:52.067 --> 23:55.557
I need a well-paid job.

23:55.557 --> 23:58.087
I'm sorry. I shouldn't have...

24:04.717 --> 24:06.437
Hey, does it hurt?

24:06.437 --> 24:07.437
Not really.

24:09.297 --> 24:13.487
You're a runaway,
aren't you? I can tell.

24:13.667 --> 24:16.797
But, you can't enjoy
Tokyo with this rain.

24:16.797 --> 24:18.777
Huh? Yeah...

24:19.297 --> 24:20.717
Come with me.

24:39.777 --> 24:42.047
Hey, it will clear up now.

24:42.047 --> 24:43.227
Huh?

24:55.497 --> 24:57.747
Hey, what do you mean...

25:13.567 --> 25:15.397
A sunshine girl!?

25:16.847 --> 25:19.247
I'm Hina. And you?

25:19.247 --> 25:19.997
Hodaka.

25:19.997 --> 25:20.837
How old are you?

25:21.397 --> 25:22.397
16.

25:23.557 --> 25:25.057
Younger than me.

25:25.057 --> 25:26.357
I will be...

25:26.357 --> 25:27.857
Hmm...

25:27.857 --> 25:29.177
18, next month.

25:29.177 --> 25:30.867
Huh? No way!

25:30.867 --> 25:33.247
You should treat me with respect.

25:40.367 --> 25:42.317
Nice to meet you, Hodaka.

25:43.747 --> 25:44.877
Yeah.

26:33.407 --> 26:34.757
Mom, there's a fish.

26:34.757 --> 26:37.067
Really? That's nice.

26:37.837 --> 26:39.587
Don't say bullshit.

26:39.587 --> 26:43.017
I'm serious. This way.

26:46.107 --> 26:47.427
Look, over there.

26:48.797 --> 26:49.847
Can't see anything.

26:49.847 --> 26:52.587
It's there. Look harder.

27:05.647 --> 27:07.477
What is that?

27:23.297 --> 27:29.687
The Kanto region is experiencing
record-breaking rainfall this summer.

27:29.687 --> 27:33.167
It has been raining
continuously for two months.

27:33.167 --> 27:38.507
The 30 days forecast predicts
more heavy rain for another month.

27:36.067 --> 27:39.067
Sunshine For You

27:38.607 --> 27:43.637
The Meteorological Agency said
it's an extremely exceptional...

27:43.577 --> 27:47.077
5000 yen

27:43.577 --> 27:47.077
Sunshine For You

27:46.487 --> 27:48.737
Too expensive?

27:48.737 --> 27:52.287
Hey, hey!
Look, it's amazing!

27:52.287 --> 27:52.907
Huh?

27:53.567 --> 27:55.737
Fell down with the
rain... something?

27:53.567 --> 27:55.737
#Rain?

27:53.567 --> 27:55.737
#Fish?

27:53.567 --> 27:55.737
#Walk

27:53.567 --> 27:55.737
#WillGoBack

27:53.567 --> 27:55.737
#SomethingFell

27:55.737 --> 27:57.237
At the Cosmo Hall parking lot.
Something fell?

27:57.237 --> 27:58.737
The fafrotskies!!
They came!!

27:57.237 --> 27:58.737
#FishFromTheSky #Fafrotskies
#SomethingFell #OhNo #Sky
#TooMuchRainNowadays #But
#ChildrenEnjoyIt #ParentingDiary
#Daughter #Child #RainyDay
#GirlOutfit

27:58.737 --> 28:01.077
A mysterious object fell from the sky.
Like a see-through jellyfish, but barely
noticeable in the water. Depending on
the angler, it seems like an organ.
Found by our good dog, Ruu

28:01.537 --> 28:03.987
They kind of look like fish.

28:04.257 --> 28:06.407
They fell from the sky?

28:06.407 --> 28:09.117
But, they left no trace...

28:09.117 --> 28:11.447
They instantly disappear.
Look at it!

28:10.077 --> 28:14.087
The Fafrotskies Phenomenon!!!!!
Is that a fish?

28:15.867 --> 28:18.547
Hey, do you remember what the
guy we interviewed said?

28:18.547 --> 28:21.617
The sky's a deeper unknown
world than the sea.

28:22.727 --> 28:26.117
A cumulonimbus can hold as
much water as a whole lake.

28:26.117 --> 28:29.727
So, it could as well harbor
an uncharted ecosystem.

28:29.727 --> 28:32.097
Like, these fish?

28:32.097 --> 28:34.407
I guess.
Amazing, isn't it?

28:34.967 --> 28:36.137
That means...

28:36.787 --> 28:38.507
We can make good money from it!

28:38.507 --> 28:39.727
Huh? What?

28:40.517 --> 28:42.817
You are starting to
sound exactly like Kei-chan.

28:42.817 --> 28:45.197
You'll be a boring grown-up.

28:45.197 --> 28:48.187
Don't put off your sunshine girl.

28:48.187 --> 28:48.987
You're going on a date, right?

28:48.987 --> 28:50.577
It's not a date, I just...

28:50.577 --> 28:52.767
I'm going to look for a job.

28:52.767 --> 28:54.777
Job? Don't you work here?

28:54.777 --> 28:56.277
I'm just hanging out.

29:01.657 --> 29:04.177
But I'm telling you, it's not a date.

29:05.657 --> 29:08.807
I understand how
you feel, Keisuke-san.

29:08.807 --> 29:12.767
But, she finally stopped
talking about you.

29:13.477 --> 29:16.567
It would be cruel
to meet her now.

29:16.567 --> 29:19.407
But... I have the right to see her.

29:19.407 --> 29:22.807
Besides, you smoke, don't you?

29:23.237 --> 29:24.037
Huh?

29:24.037 --> 29:26.377
She's got asthma.

29:26.377 --> 29:28.307
You're too inconsiderate.

29:28.307 --> 29:31.727
I... quit smoking...
a little while ago.

29:31.727 --> 29:33.587
But...

29:33.587 --> 29:36.197
You give a bad impression.

29:45.887 --> 29:48.107
It's raining all the time this year.

29:48.107 --> 29:51.997
She can't play outside,
and it's bad for her asthma.

29:53.017 --> 29:55.577
I feel sorry for
children nowadays.

29:55.577 --> 29:58.957
We used to have beautiful
springs and summers.

30:11.437 --> 30:13.967
They can't live together,
just the two of them.

30:13.967 --> 30:15.467
You're right...

30:22.207 --> 30:23.297
Wait a second...

30:24.387 --> 30:26.517
Can it be that...

30:27.157 --> 30:30.677
that I'm visiting a girl's home...

30:30.967 --> 30:33.077
for the first time!

30:34.477 --> 30:37.117
Welcome, Hodaka.
Did you get lost?

30:37.117 --> 30:39.667
No, uhm...
It's not much, but...

30:39.667 --> 30:43.167
Thank you for it.
Come in.

30:43.617 --> 30:44.597
Thank you.

