42:10.927 --> 42:13.927
"Sky Fish" report

42:10.927 --> 42:13.927
Visit to the meteorological lab

42:10.927 --> 42:13.927
Fish from the sky? #1

42:10.927 --> 42:13.927
Fish from the sky? #2

42:10.927 --> 42:13.927
By chance sunshine in Odaiba?

42:18.337 --> 42:22.647
Oh, that project?
Right, we've put it on hold.

42:22.647 --> 42:25.457
Sorry, we're not going ahead with it.

42:25.457 --> 42:31.057
I see... Yeah, I'll do my best
 so please call us again.

42:41.677 --> 42:42.727
What?

42:56.237 --> 42:58.167
Hello, Mamiya speaking.

42:58.167 --> 43:00.487
Mamiya-san, It's Keisuke.

43:00.487 --> 43:03.687
Sorry to rush you.
Regarding out meeting...

43:04.967 --> 43:09.377
You're late, Kei-chan!
It's an important interview.

43:09.377 --> 43:12.387
Are we in a bad mood?
No luck with work?

43:12.387 --> 43:13.497
Where's Hodaka?

43:15.297 --> 43:16.887
Busy with his other job?

43:16.817 --> 43:19.317
Su

43:16.817 --> 43:19.317
Ho

43:17.817 --> 43:19.597
He's neglecting work lately.

43:19.597 --> 43:22.607
Just let him be.
We're not that busy.

43:22.607 --> 43:24.697
He took in that cat.

43:24.697 --> 43:26.307
You did the same
with him, Kei-chan.

43:26.307 --> 43:26.947
Huh?

43:26.947 --> 43:30.627
You helped him because he
reminded you of yourself.

43:31.807 --> 43:35.877
How much are you paying for Hodaka-kun?

43:35.877 --> 43:38.627
Only 30.000 yen?
That's so low.

43:38.627 --> 43:40.637
Nope. It's 3.000.

43:40.637 --> 43:42.027
What?

43:42.027 --> 43:45.407
Are you serious? 3.000 yen a month?
That's exploitation!

43:45.407 --> 43:45.867
Look ahead.

43:45.867 --> 43:51.237
You're gonna get sued! Actually, I will
report you to the Labor Standards Bureau!

43:51.237 --> 43:57.227
He gets free food and accommodation,
and the company pays his phone bills...

43:57.227 --> 43:58.537
Ugh!

43:59.917 --> 44:02.317
No wonder he's
got an extra job.

44:04.737 --> 44:08.547
I am surprised.
It really cleared up.

44:09.047 --> 44:13.057
You kids are amazing.
It's a shame you're quitting.

44:13.057 --> 44:16.987
She was caught on camera.
We got flooded with requests.

44:13.877 --> 44:16.877
The web famous Sunshine Girl!?

44:13.877 --> 44:16.877
Jingu Gaien Fireworks Festival

44:16.987 --> 44:19.057
We really can't do it anymore.

44:19.057 --> 44:23.067
We'll do one more and
then stop for a while...

44:23.667 --> 44:27.067
She looks tired, too.

44:28.437 --> 44:30.367
Got guests, Granny?

44:30.367 --> 44:31.987
Oh, you're right here.

44:31.987 --> 44:34.077
I came to help.

44:34.077 --> 44:37.577
Very young guests.
Are you Granny's friends?

44:37.577 --> 44:38.617
Hello!

44:38.877 --> 44:42.537
I've asked for nice weather on
my husband's first anniversary.

44:42.537 --> 44:44.977
It stopped raining, in fact!

44:52.197 --> 44:55.897
It'd be hard for him to come
back if it was raining.

44:55.897 --> 44:56.967
"Come back"?

44:56.967 --> 45:01.107
They say the dead come back
from the sky around Obon, in August.

45:01.607 --> 45:05.707
So that means, it's
his first Obon after he died?

45:05.707 --> 45:06.707
Yes.

45:06.707 --> 45:09.107
So that's my mom's
first Obon too.

45:10.527 --> 45:13.617
You've lost your mother last year?

45:14.217 --> 45:15.127
Yes.

45:15.127 --> 45:21.137
Light a welcoming fire for her.
She will protect you.

45:21.537 --> 45:22.587
Thanks.

45:26.927 --> 45:31.637
Riding the smoke, he will
come back from the other side.

45:31.637 --> 45:32.937
From where?

45:32.937 --> 45:34.637
From heaven.

45:35.437 --> 45:39.447
There's always been another
world, up in the sky.

45:43.757 --> 45:48.147
Apparently, this is what the
Weather Maiden saw.

45:48.407 --> 45:50.247
It's a mysterious painting.

45:50.247 --> 45:52.967
Flying fish in the sky.
And even a dragon.

45:52.967 --> 45:54.757
It's beautiful.

45:54.757 --> 45:56.357
Right?

45:56.357 --> 46:00.867
And this "Weather Maiden"?
They were like a shaman, right?

46:00.867 --> 46:02.777
Huh? What?

46:02.777 --> 46:05.827
Were they like a shaman?

46:05.827 --> 46:07.207
Yeah.

46:08.287 --> 46:12.887
Fixing the weather
is the Maiden's job.

46:12.887 --> 46:14.657
Fixing it?

46:14.677 --> 46:15.827
Sounds fishy to me.

46:15.827 --> 46:19.257
Like this year's
abnormal weather?

46:19.257 --> 46:23.237
There's nothing abnormal about that.

46:23.237 --> 46:29.017
They keep saying the same thing.
"First time in the recorded history"

46:29.017 --> 46:33.477
But when did records begin?
Maybe 100 years ago at best.

46:33.477 --> 46:36.327
How old do you think this is?

46:36.567 --> 46:38.267
800 years old!

46:38.267 --> 46:38.867
800??

46:40.047 --> 46:42.377
Don't get too excited, Grandpa.

46:45.337 --> 46:48.887
In the first place... the
weather changes on a whim.

46:48.887 --> 46:51.167
Regardless of human needs.

46:51.167 --> 46:54.077
We can't even
tell what's the norm and what isn't.

46:54.077 --> 47:00.257
We are only allowed to stay temporarily
in the space between the sky and earth,

47:00.257 --> 47:05.067
clinging hard not
to be shaken off...

47:05.067 --> 47:09.557
You know, we used
to know this in the past.

47:10.837 --> 47:16.647
However, there's a thin thread
linking us humans and the sky.

47:17.657 --> 47:20.487
The Weather Maiden.

47:19.557 --> 47:26.817
{=0\b1\frz2.793\fscx62\fscy62\move(280.6,635.6,-40.33,635.58,30,7238)}I'd like
sunshine
for our
wedding!!

